WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.960 --> 00:00:11.040
Here we will use the Short Match functionality in&nbsp;
the UCSC Genome Browser to find a short sequence

00:00:11.040 --> 00:00:17.600
motif within our contig. Before we get started, go&nbsp;
to the Genome Browser Gateway page and select the

00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:24.560
D. melanogaster genome and the August 2014 BDGP
Release 6 + ISO1 MT/dm6 assembly. Enter

00:00:24.560 --> 00:00:43.040
chr2r:18,867,350 -18,867,430 into&nbsp;
the search term field and click submit.

00:00:43.760 --> 00:00:51.280
This region contains the transcription start site&nbsp;
of the Drosophila melanogaster DptB gene. Short

00:00:51.280 --> 00:00:57.920
match can be used to search for short sequences&nbsp;
between 2 and 30 bases long. For this example, we

00:00:57.920 --> 00:01:05.120
will use short match to search for the initiator&nbsp;
motif or Inr. The Inr is a motif that is associated

00:01:05.120 --> 00:01:11.360
with the RNA polymerase II core promoter and&nbsp;
previous studies suggest that transcription factor

00:01:11.360 --> 00:01:21.520
IID or TFIID binds specifically to this motif. The&nbsp;
Inr motif when found typically begins two bases

00:01:21.520 --> 00:01:27.840
upstream of the transcription start site though&nbsp;
the location of the motif can vary by a few bases.

00:01:28.560 --> 00:01:34.240
The consensus sequence for the Inr motif in&nbsp;
Drosophila is six bases long running in the

00:01:34.240 --> 00:01:40.080
same orientation as the gene. To use Short&nbsp;
Match, locate the Mapping and Sequencing

00:01:40.080 --> 00:01:45.040
Tracks section within the Genome Browser&nbsp;
and click on the Short Match link. Change

00:01:45.040 --> 00:01:53.840
the Display mode field to "pack" and type TCAKTY
into the Short 2-30 base sequence field.

00:01:54.720 --> 00:02:00.480
Note that TCAKTY is the consensus&nbsp;
sequence for the Inr in Drosophila.

00:02:01.120 --> 00:02:09.680
K represents keto, either guanine or thymine, and Y&nbsp;
represents pyrimidine, either cytosine or thymine.

00:02:09.680 --> 00:02:15.680
After changing the display mode and typing&nbsp;
in the consensus sequence, click submit. You

00:02:15.680 --> 00:02:20.880
will see Perfect Matches to the Short Sequence&nbsp;
that you typed appear as black bars within the

00:02:20.880 --> 00:02:26.720
browser window. The label next to the black&nbsp;
bar describes the orientation and the start

00:02:26.720 --> 00:02:34.560
position of the motif match. In this case, the Inr&nbsp;
motif is located three nucleotides downstream

00:02:34.560 --> 00:02:48.960
of the annotated transcription start site of&nbsp;
DptB at 18,867,394 in the positive orientation.

